The end is very bitter and it is concluded in October 1988. Cardinal Erdw. Cassidy dared to inform a Pope for the first time, who was in this instance John Paul II, who became angry and then depressed. He immediately convened a very small nucleus of cardinals who learned of the fraud.
Cardinal Tomko was in favour of telling the truth since it will not be possible to change the Sindon. John Paul timidly supported his position while Cardinal Ratzinguer firmly opposed it, alleging extremely serious reasons of scandal.
In addition, there remain moreover the reasons which provoked the imposture, the discovery that there had been no death on the cross. The motive was extremely serious and the decision to lock down the scandal was imperative, its disclosure being bound to trigger it immediately, contrary to what happens in similar circumstances. It was Cardinal Ballestrero who was charged with delivering a sample of the fabric to the laboratories.
